course: dictionary
lesson: 12622
title: Loyal and disloyal
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Loyal means you stick by your friends, family, team or country, even when it is hard. The prefix dis- turns it into the opposite, so disloyal means not loyal. Look for dis- at the start of a word: it often means "not".
explain: «Sam told the other team our secret plan, so he was disloyal to his own team.» The words told the other team show that Sam did not support his team. The clue is in what he did.
explain: Disloyal can also describe a character in a story. «The knight was disloyal and secretly fought for the enemy king.» A knight is meant to serve his own king faithfully, so the word tells you he broke that promise.
fact: Loyal means faithful and supporting.
fact: Disloyal means not loyal: not supporting or being faithful to your friends, family, team or country.
fact: The prefix dis- often means "not" or "the opposite", as in dislike and disagree.
fact: «Disloyal» is an adjective, so it describes a person: «a disloyal friend».
fact: In stories about ethics, friendship and history, being disloyal often breaks trust.
exercise: «The disloyal soldier secretly gave the castle keys to the enemy.» What does disloyal mean here? | *Not faithful to his own side | Very tall | Tired after a long march | Very brave in battle
exercise: What is the opposite of disloyal? | Lazy | *Loyal | Noisy | Mean
exercise: «Ben stayed with his team even when they were losing, so he was never disloyal.» What does this tell you about Ben? | He left the team when it got hard | *He stayed faithful to his team | He wanted a new team | He broke the team rules
test: Which sentence shows someone being disloyal? | «Mia kept her best friend's secret safe.» | *«Jake told everyone his best friend's secret.» | «Ravi cheered for his school at the match.»
test: The prefix dis- in disloyal means... | Before | *Not | Very | Again
exam: Which best describes a disloyal friend? | One who likes football | One who lives far away | One who is always early | *One who lets you down or betrays you
